      "title": "RULE vs NOOTROPIC",
      "text": "RULE is the better fit for focus, while NOOTROPIC is the better fit for focus.\nLion's Mane: RULE 800 mg; NOOTROPIC 500 mg.\nEria Jarensis: RULE 150 mg; NOOTROPIC 125 mg.\nMucuna Pruriens: RULE 100 mg; NOOTROPIC 70 mg.\nOnly RULE discloses: Alpha GPC: 600 mg per 2 scoops; Dendrobium Extract: 300 mg per 2 scoops; Uridine Monophosphate: 250 mg per 2 scoops; Theobromine: 200 mg per 2 scoops; Cafe Alatus: 100 mg per 2 scoops; L-Theanine: 100 mg per 2 scoops; Bitter Orange Extract: 80 mg per 2 scoops; Dicaffeine Malate: 50 mg per 2 scoops.\nOnly NOOTROPIC discloses: Sodium Bicarbonate: 500 mg per full serving; Alpha GPC 50%: 600 mg per full serving; Dendrobium Extract 10:1: 300 mg per full serving; GABA: 100 mg per full serving; Dextrose: 1000 mg per full serving; AstraGin: 25 mg per full serving.\nRULE caffeine: RULE officially lists 485 mg total caffeine per 2 scoops; 1-scoop option also shown. NOOTROPIC caffeine: NOOTROPIC officially lists 350 mg total caffeine per 1 scoop.\nRULE: RULE: A hyper-focus pre-workout positioned around concentrated nootropic support, controlled focus, energy, and performance. The easiest concrete points are 485 mg official total caffeine at two scoops, 3 g L-Tyrosine, Lion's Mane and Uridine. NOOTROPIC: NOOTROPIC: A high-focus pre-workout positioned around cognitive support, energy, and pump. The easiest concrete points are 350 mg caffeine anhydrous, Lion's Mane and Alpha GPC positioning, Four represented flavors.\nMatch the recommendation to the buyer’s primary goal: RULE for focus; NOOTROPIC for focus.",
