      "text": "NOOTROPIC is the better fit for focus, while BUMP is the better fit for focus.\nGABA: NOOTROPIC 100 mg; BUMP 500 mg.\nCaffeine Anhydrous: NOOTROPIC 350 mg; BUMP 80 mg.\nOnly NOOTROPIC discloses: Beta-Alanine: 3200 mg per full serving; L-Citrulline: 3000 mg per full serving; Sodium Bicarbonate: 500 mg per full serving; Pink Himalayan Salt: 300 mg per full serving; Alpha GPC 50%: 600 mg per full serving; Dendrobium Extract 10:1: 300 mg per full serving; Eria Jarensis: 125 mg per full serving; Mucuna Pruriens: 70 mg per full serving.\nOnly BUMP discloses: Taurine: 2 g per 2 scoops; Alpha GPC: 600 mg per 2 scoops; Uridine Monophosphate: 100 mg per 2 scoops; 5-HTP: 100 mg per 2 scoops; Natural Caffeine: 80 mg per 2 scoops; L-Theanine: 80 mg per 2 scoops; Bitter Orange Extract: 60 mg per 2 scoops; PEAKO2: 20 mg per 2 scoops.\nNOOTROPIC caffeine: NOOTROPIC officially lists 350 mg total caffeine per 1 scoop. BUMP caffeine: BUMP lists stimulant ingredients, but the verified source set does not confirm a total caffeine amount.\nNOOTROPIC: NOOTROPIC: A high-focus pre-workout positioned around cognitive support, energy, and pump. The easiest concrete points are 350 mg caffeine anhydrous, Lion's Mane and Alpha GPC positioning, Four represented flavors. BUMP: BUMP: A lower-stimulant nootropic drink positioned for work, gaming, and daily mental focus rather than a full high-stim pre-workout. The easiest concrete points are Nootropic-first daily positioning, Lower-stimulant placement, Two represented flavors.\nMatch the recommendation to the buyer’s primary goal: NOOTROPIC for focus; BUMP for focus.",
